    "expect_check": "aav.sc_capacity",
    "expect_severity": "fail",
    "rationale": "A 3,000 bp cassette that is entirely legal as a single stranded genome, 1,700 bp under the 4,700 bp target, but is declared self complementary. A self complementary genome is an inverted repeat of the cassette, so the capsid has to hold roughly twice the length and the usable capacity halves: 3,000 bp is 600 bp over the 2,400 bp self complementary target and 400 bp over the 2,600 bp hard ceiling. aav.sc_capacity is the check that must catch it, and aav.packaging_limit must NOT fail, because the length is fine for the single stranded modality it is not using. That split is the whole point of the case: it proves the halved band is applied to the right designs and that the failure names the reason. The payload is a length-calibrated tandem concatenation of whole in-frame copies of the real beta-lactamase reading frame of pUC19, GenBank L09137.1 (tests/fixtures/parser/puc19.gb) with one terminal stop codon, assembled only to put the cassette at the exact length this case is about. It is not a real gene and nothing here presents it as one; the defect under test is the length, not the payload.",
